rom two timer pins, clamp + AC-coupled receive tap" (at 21.5 201 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left)) (uuid 6932cb64-4bf9-4a83-a877-f513d047f8c5)) (rectangle (start 178 198) (end 330 445) (stroke (width 0.2) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid e12677d5-8ea2-4f89-870f-93452960a8d4)) (text "RECEIVE CHAIN: input mux, 2 x OPA356 (x10 each), gain-select mux, ADC anti-alias" (at 179.5 201 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left)) (uuid 1ec2cd35-d23e-445a-830c-cc45d7cefbc9)) (rectangle (start 20 451) (end 172 533) (stroke (width 0.2) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid 72711212-78d8-4979-b422-0f6cd551ae77)) (text "ALARM, LED, BUTTON" (at 21.5 454 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left)) (uuid e6b1e0d1-eb9a-42ce-be9d-8e6c79d262c8)) (rectangle (start 178 451) (end 330 533) (stroke (width 0.2) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid 9e8c0e57-16d5-445c-a47a-76751746680a)) (text "OLED, UART, SWD" (at 179.5 454 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left)) (uuid d83dc466-c20f-4ba0-8991-7942b38397ed)) (text "Measurement: STM32 TIM3 makes a 6-cycle 1 MHz burst on two pins (second inverted = bridge drive, 6.6 Vpp) into transducer A; transducer B receives through U4/LNA/U7 into ADC1 at 4 MS/s (64 samples DMA). Then roles swap. 1000 up/down pairs per measurement." (at 20 280 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid 0e039d5e-73d1-4850-9ad7-980f2aa0a311)) (text "While receiving, one leg of the transducer is held low by its timer pin and the other is high-impedance and feeds the clamp + mux. LNA1 x10.2 (20 dB), LNA2 x10 (+20 dB), U7 selects 20 or 40 dB." (at 20 287 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid 6ecc53e7-dcd5-4c8d-91ae-245d488fb7cd)) (text "2-layer prototype. Production should use 4 layers (solid analog ground, guarded receive trace) - see docs." (at 20 294 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left)) (uuid 00b02802-7174-444c-b2ee-87d2544e39d8)) (sheet_instances (path "/" (page "1"))))